        <mxCell id="p4-legend" value="&lt;b&gt;Nodes&lt;/b&gt;: demand — S+7 feats: static (shift one-hot S dims, kind 0=min/1=capacity, day position in year, special-day flag) + dynamic, refreshed at each day boundary (filled flag via env.slot_filled, already-passed flag). Dashed border = kind &#39;cap&#39;; &lt;font color=&quot;#cc0000&quot;&gt;red outline = demand node currently being decided (demand_ids = slot-queue index) — its embedding is the slot context fed to the heads&lt;/font&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Edges (all static, precomputed once per scenario)&lt;/b&gt;: &lt;font color=&quot;#82b366&quot;&gt;green = employee ↔ team&lt;/font&gt; · &lt;font color=&quot;#d79b00&quot;&gt;orange = demand belongs_to / has_demand team&lt;/font&gt; · &lt;font color=&quot;#9673a6&quot;&gt;purple dashed = qualified / qualified_by (team membership + not on vacation — e.g. E2 is on vacation on Day 2, so no edge to the Day-2 Team-A slot)&lt;/font&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;GNN&lt;/b&gt;: day_proj → demand_proj; conv over the 6 static relations; the policy sees a slot-specific neighborhood (its qualified employees + team) instead of a day-level average." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
